# CODEOWNERS — CI-critical paths (007.003-T / U3)
#
# Partially resolves stash BEDD2E70. Does NOT close the self-modifying-PR
# gap: `pull_request` workflows execute from the PR's own proposed head, so
# a PR touching these paths can still edit the very workflow/scripts that
# validate it and make its own required check succeed. Advisory CODEOWNERS
# review has no enforcement effect against that on its own. This file ships
# OWNERSHIP METADATA — a prerequisite for a future control, not the control
# itself. The residual self-modifying-PR gap remains an explicit open
# operator decision.
#
# ADVISORY METADATA ONLY (NON-NEGOTIABLE, see docs/plans/
# 2026-09-04-intercom-go-ci-supply-chain-hardening-plan.md, risk R1): this
# file has NO enforcement effect until branch protection or a repository
# ruleset explicitly enables "Require review from Code Owners" on `main`.
# THAT IS A SEPARATE, DELIBERATE OPERATOR ACTION — this unit does not take
# it, and verified at implementation time that no repository or
# organization ruleset / branch protection rule already enables it (if one
# had, creating this file would have newly matched an owner and been
# expected to deadlock unattended merges awaiting a review that, under dark
# -factory/unattended operation, is not coming;
# `merge_approval_pre_authorized` satisfies the harness's own merge gate,
# never a GitHub branch-protection code-owner-review requirement). Before
# ever flipping code-owner review to required, first provision an approval
# path for unattended PRs (see risk R1 in the plan above) — otherwise every
# dark-factory PR touching the paths below will block forever awaiting a
# human review.
#
# Every owner below was verified to resolve to a real account with repo
# access at authoring time (`gh api users/softwaresalt`) — a dangling owner
# silently disables the rule it's attached to, producing the appearance of
# a control with none of the effect.
#
# Covers ALL CI-critical scripts and workflow surfaces, or none (partial
# ownership coverage here would be a misleading control). "CI-critical"
# here means executable gate/workflow logic and the ownership file itself.
# /.github/constraints/ is included: it is the hash-pin trust boundary this
# shipment builds (007.001-T) and is exactly as CI-critical as the
# workflows that consume it. scripts/testdata/gitignore/** (fixture DATA,
# not executable gate logic) is deliberately NOT listed here -- it is
# committed test input, not a CI-critical script or workflow surface.

/.github/workflows/                          @softwaresalt
/.github/CODEOWNERS                          @softwaresalt
/.github/constraints/                        @softwaresalt
/scripts/ci-topology-check.sh                @softwaresalt
/scripts/check-retired-architecture.sh       @softwaresalt
/scripts/check-gitignore-append-only.sh      @softwaresalt
